-- title:
--   Image of a homomorphism is an abelian subvariety
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $f : J \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be a scheme over $k$ carrying a relative group law $L$, that is, functorial multiplication, unit and inversion operations on the sets $\{\varphi : T \to J \mid \varphi \circ f = t\}$ of sections over arbitrary $k$-schemes $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, satisfying associativity, the unit laws, left inversion and compatibility with base change along $k$-morphisms $T' \to T$. Assume $f$ satisfies `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle`, i.e. $f$ is smooth and proper, each fibre of $f$ over a point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ is connected, and $f$ admits some relative group law; assume moreover that $L$ is commutative on $T$-sections for every $T$. Let $g : X \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper and geometrically reduced with $X$ connected, equipped with a relative group law $L_X$, and let $\sigma : X \to J$ satisfy $\sigma \circ g$-compatibility, i.e. $\sigma$ followed by $f$ equals $g$, and be a homomorphism: for all $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and all $T$-sections $x,y$ of $g$, the composite of $L_X.\mathrm{mul}\,t\,x\,y$ with $\sigma$ equals $L.\mathrm{mul}$ of the composites of $x$ and of $y$ with $\sigma$. Write $B \hookrightarrow J$ for the scheme-theoretic image inclusion $\sigma.\mathrm{imageι}$ of $\sigma$, viewed as a $k$-scheme via $\sigma.\mathrm{imageι}$ followed by $f$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a relative group law $L_B$ on this $k$-scheme such that: $L_B$ again satisfies `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle` (smooth, proper, connected fibres, group law present); $L_B$ is commutative on $T$-sections for every $T$; the inclusion $B \to J$ is a homomorphism from $L_B$ to $L$ on $T$-sections; and for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ that is a $k$-algebra, a section $z$ of $f$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $k \to \Omega$ factors through $B \to J$ if and only if it factors as $\sigma$ composed with some $\Omega$-section of $g$.
--
--   This is the statement that the scheme-theoretic image of a homomorphism from a proper geometrically reduced connected group-law scheme into an abelian variety over a field is again an abelian variety, a closed subgroup whose points over any algebraically closed extension are exactly the images of the points of the source; classically it is the case over a field of the theorem that the image of a homomorphism of group schemes of finite type is a closed subgroup scheme. It is used to produce the abelian subvariety generated by a family of endomorphisms and, through that, in the study of endomorphism degrees for fake elliptic curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GoodReductionJacobian_RelativeGroupLaw_exists_relativeGroupLaw_image_of_homomorphism.lean

import Mathlib
